where we have confidence.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.120
So that means
confidence in the code,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.160
confidence in making
changes to the code,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.560
confidence in having it
out in the wild, making

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.840
sure it's running well,
confidence that if something

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.320
goes down, I will fix it-- or I
will know about it-- confidence

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.590
that someone else will
fix it, in all likelihood.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.720
These are all things we
have to be confident about.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.090
And this is the general
theme of this presentation.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.910
How do we go from starting
a project to having it

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:31.980
in production, live, costing
us a lot of money, confidently?

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.810
And this is broken down
into six core segments.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.810
First thing we're going
to talk about, briefly--

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.640
code.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.675
How to make good code.

00:02:38.675 --> 00:02:41.050
Some things about serverless
that I think a lot of people

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.234
get wrong when they're
thinking about code.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.400
Then we're going to go into
testing and general talk

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.340
about how we think about
testing in serverless.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.200
We'll go into
deployments and rollback,

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.741
some of the tools,
some of the things

00:02:51.741 --> 00:02:54.970
we announced this week about
how to do deployments better,

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.910
how to fix issues when you
deploy something broken.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.070
Because regardless of
how good your tests are,

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.450
there's still a pretty
good chance something

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.220
bad will get into
production eventually,

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.050
so we want to prepare for that.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.420
Then we'll move on to
configuration, environments,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.420
dealing with staging
environments and production

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.940
environments, how to think about
how your code relates to that.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.620
Then we'll move
into monitoring, how

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.570
to keep an eye on
what's happening, how

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.902
to know if something breaks,
how to feel confident

00:03:18.902 --> 00:03:20.860
that if something breaks,
you'll hear about it,

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.140
preferably before
your consumers do.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.150
And then we'll move
into figuring out

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.580
how much stuff costs,
dealing with predictability

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.510
in our pricing and all of
